        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/l/f4b2a3/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2025-12-08T21:16:41.901Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Life Day With Lobe’Haka</p>\n<p>The prime wardens photo could be placed with a bunch of people from the 17th through 20th centuries that are definitely dead by now, but Haka wasn’t around for their death, he just knew them for a while and then lost track of them, but after no contact for a year or twenty, he just assumed they had exited his life, and he began to mourn them, not as being dead but just as gone, and he’s counting the PW in that category at this point.</p>\n<p>Pre-OblivAeon, Haka’s biggest hit would be +39 from Haka of Battle on top of a Savage Mana that has consumed all 13 Endlings from the Enclave, plus the largest number of villain targets in any deck, I’m not sure what that is but let’s call it 17 for argument.  So that’s 99 damage, I hope 17 is the actual limit because that would be perfect.  So Pre-OblivAeon, Haka maxes out the 2-digit field, and then he can pick up an Oblivion Shard and consume the entire Aeon Man deck and get well into the triple digits, maybe 150 if you survive long enough.</p>",
        "post_number": 7,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2025-12-09T10:51:58.696Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
